== the report: paragraph mode
1: a|b
2: c|d
== paragraph: leading blank lines skipped, blank lines in a row are one separator, a line of spaces is not blank, RT
1 NF=4 [p1 l1\np1 l2] RT=[\n\n\n\n]
2 NF=4 [p2 l1\n  \np2 l3] RT=[\n\n]
== paragraph: input without a final newline; with one
1: [x\ny] RT=[\n\n]
2: [z] RT=[]
1: [c\nd] RT=[\n]
== paragraph: newline separates fields whatever FS is
1: NF=4 a,b,c,d
2: NF=2 e,f,,
regex FS: NF=3
1=[a]
2=[b]
3=[c
d]
default FS: NF=3
== split() in paragraph mode
split: 2
1=[a]
2=[b\nc]
== one character
1: [a] RT=[;]
2: [b] RT=[;]
3: [] RT=[;]
4: [c\n] RT=[]
1: a
2: b
3: c
1: [a]
2: [b]
3: []
4: [c]
== a regular expression
1: [a] RT=[12]
2: [b] RT=[345]
3: [c\n] RT=[]
1: [one] length=3
2: [two] length=3
3: [three] length=5
3 c
== RS by -v, and as an operand between files
f1: 1: p
f1: 2: r
f1: 1: p
q
f1: 2: r
f2: 1: u
f2: 2: v
f2: 3: w
== RS changed between records
1: [a]
2: [b]
3: [c]
4: [d\ne\n]
1: [p1\np2]
2: [q1]
3: [q2]
1: [r1]
2: [r2]
3: [r3]
== getline and getline < file follow RS
after getline: m2
f2: [u]
f2: [v]
f2: [w]
== a separator split between two reads (a pipe that hands over the rest a second later) is one separator
1: [a] RT=[\n\n\n\n]
2: [b] RT=[\n]
1: [a] RT=[1234]
2: [b\n] RT=[]
== a long input: records across reads
4286 line 30000
4286 29996
30001
